 "intro": {
  "title": "THE RELIQUARY ROAD",
  "lines": [
   "The road to the Deep is lined with graves.",
   "Every one of them is from somewhere else."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "Next: the Chitin Aqueduct. The only water on the world that still moves.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [29, 114],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A road lined with graves. Not mounds: slabs stood on end with a bronze band across them, in rows. Somebody sweeps them. The bronze is bright."
  },
  {
   "id": "arches",
   "at": [29, 100],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The roofed arches have walls: nothing shoots down into them. The open stretches between are the long shots. The wall panels beside you will open."
  },
  {
   "id": "tools",
   "at": [20, 108],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Hand tools, a whole chapel of them: planes, saws, chisels, one pattern, thousands, hung in rows. They made everything with the same few things."
  },
  {
   "id": "clocks",
   "at": [40, 96],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A clock on every grave, and no two agree. Somebody wound them all, once. Nobody has since."
  },
  {
   "id": "plate1",
   "at": [29, 90],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "Run a nail down it: one number, 211,408, and a short falling note. The same number is on the slab beside it, and the one beside that."
  },
  {
   "id": "boots",
   "at": [20, 80],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Boots in pairs, a pair to a grave, laced. The pairs go small, large, small."
  },
  {
   "id": "lamps",
   "at": [40, 62],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Lamps: brass, glass, clay, a hundred ways of holding a flame. They liked to see what they were doing."
  },
  {
   "id": "nets",
   "at": [20, 46],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Nets, folded, a net to a grave, folded the way you fold one you mean to use again."
  },
  {
   "id": "strings",
   "at": [40, 30],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Stringed instruments, one to a grave, and every string cut."
  },
